course: dictionary
lesson: 9240
title: Words with two faces
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. «A sop to voters» is about politics, not food: a politician gives voters a small treat to keep them happy, without really solving their problem. Read the words around sop to find its meaning.
explain: «Her coat was sopping wet» means soaking wet, like a towel after a swim. The word wet is the clue, and sopping is a stronger way of saying very wet. Swap your meaning into the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have probably got it.
explain: Some words look like other words. «Mistakes like reading «shop» as «sop» are normal: the child read the s and missed its partner h.» Slow, careful reading helps you spot every letter that is really there.
fact: A sop is something small given to calm someone down or keep them quiet, without really fixing the problem.
fact: «A sop to voters» means a small gift meant to please them.
fact: «Sopping wet» means soaking wet, and it is very common in the UK and Ireland.
fact: Old use: a sop is a piece of bread soaked in milk, soup or gravy.
fact: As a verb, «sop up» means to soak up liquid with bread or a cloth. It is rare.
exercise: «The angry fans were given a sop to calm them down.» What is a sop here? | A loud shout | A large bowl of soup | *A small gift to keep them quiet | A pair of shoes
exercise: «Her coat was sopping wet after the rain.» What does sopping mean? | *Soaking wet | Dry and warm | Shiny and new | Torn at the edges
exercise: «Use a piece of bread to sop up the gravy.» What does sop up mean? | *Soak up the liquid | Cut the bread into squares | Throw the bread away | Dance around the table
test: In old times, a sop was a piece of bread soaked in milk, soup or gravy. What was a sop in that sense? | A type of hat | A sheet of paper | A loud noise | *A piece of bread soaked in milk, soup or gravy
test: «Mistakes like reading «shop» as «sop» are normal.» What is the best tip from this sentence? | Skip every short word you meet | Always guess the first word | Sop and shop mean exactly the same | *Read every letter carefully, because shop and sop look alike
exam: Which sentence uses sop to mean a small gift to calm someone? | The cook gave the soup to the dog. | *The council offered a small sop to the angry parents. | The rain was so heavy that the road flooded. | She put the bread in the oven to toast.
